    "exposure": {
      "locked": false,
      "form": "a scene gain through a sigmoid tone curve, per channel: G·y / (1 + (G − 1)·y/white) with G = 2^(ev * stopsPerUnit); tangent continuation above white and below 0",
      "coefficients": {
        "stopsPerUnit": 1.622202,
        "white": 1.095133
      }
    },
    "whiteBalance": {
      "locked": false,
      "form": "per-channel scene gains from the mired and tint differences to as-shot, each channel through the tone curve as in exposure (G*y / (1 + (G-1)*y/white)): r: 2^(dM*redPerMired + dTint*redPerTint), g: 2^(-dTint*greenPerTint), b: 2^(-dM*bluePerMired + dTint*bluePerTint); divided by their luma first when preserveLuma is 1",
      "coefficients": {
        "redPerMired": 0.011567,
        "bluePerMired": 0.012011,
        "greenPerTint": 0.002048,
        "redPerTint": 0.010088,
        "bluePerTint": 0.014052,
        "white": 1.085448,
        "preserveLuma": 0
      }
    },
    "whitesBlacks": {
      "locked": false,
      "form": "Whites: per channel in perceptual p = x^(1/gamma): p += whites*whitesPerUnit * p^whitesPower. Blacks, after: LightCraft Process V4 Blacks (MIT, ArtCraft Team and the LightCraft contributors; numbers from its tools/light_v3_fits/blacks.json, sign-wise tau/q exponentiated, mix weights through the sigmoid): on linear ProPhoto through the sRGB curve, F(v) = max(0, v + a*D(v)), D on knots 0,.02,.05,.09,.14,.2,.28,.38,.5,.65,.82,1 (blacksUp0..10 / blacksDown0..10, D(1) = 0), a = +-((1-exp(-t/tau))/(1-exp(-1/tau)))^q, t = |blacks|/100; per channel and on luminance, blended in linear light by blacksUpPerChannel / blacksDownPerChannel",
      "coefficients": {"whitesPerUnit": 0.001885, "whitesPower": 1.000055, "blacksUp0": 0.00167487, "blacksUp1": 0.03212663, "blacksUp2": 0.07188513, "blacksUp3": 0.09530584, "blacksUp4": 0.12925288, "blacksUp5": 0.12680973, "blacksUp6": 0.10913227, "blacksUp7": 0.10024857, "blacksUp8": 0.08351985, "blacksUp9": 0.05136152, "blacksUp10": 0.02045048, "blacksDown0": 0.00011845, "blacksDown1": 0.27066232, "blacksDown2": 0.42355931, "blacksDown3": 0.37893059, "blacksDown4": 0.22045052, "blacksDown5": 0.20955478, "blacksDown6": 0.2107909, "blacksDown7": 0.16685612, "blacksDown8": 0.13055497, "blacksDown9": 0.08667136, "blacksDown10": 0.03499726, "blacksUpTau": 1000.0, "blacksUpQ": 1.127494, "blacksDownTau": 924.998327, "blacksDownQ": 1.814141, "blacksUpPerChannel": 0.645839, "blacksDownPerChannel": 1.0}
    },
    "tone": {
      "locked": false,
      "form": "a local exposure through the tone curve, relative to the photo. base = gaussian blur of luma (radiusFraction of the long edge). The photo's anchor (256 px develop): mean A = 2^mean(log2 luma), pushed through exposure; spread = std of log2 luma; bright = share of pixels above L* 80. high H = the 95th percentile of luma, pushed through exposure like A. ps = perceptual(base*(0.18/A)^shadowsAdapt*2^(shadowsHighAdapt*(highCentre-log2 H))), ph = perceptual(base*(0.18/A)^highlightsAdapt*2^(highlightsHighAdapt*(highCentre-log2 H))); G = 2^(shadows*shadowsStopsPerUnit*exp(shadowsBright*(bright-brightCentre) + shadowsSpread*(spread-spreadCentre))*exp(-ps/shadowsTau) + highlights*highlightsStopsPerUnit*exp(highlightsMean*(log2 A-meanCentre) + highlightsSpread*(spread-spreadCentre))*min(1, ph/highlightsKnee)), each strength factor kept in [0.25, 4]; detail (luma/base)^(detailGain-1) re-applied; then per channel G*y / (1 + (G-1)*y/white) as in exposure",
      "coefficients": {
        "radiusFraction": 0.002,
        "shadowsStopsPerUnit": 0.035777,
        "shadowsTau": 0.264622,
        "shadowsAdapt": 0,
        "shadowsHighAdapt": 2.449872,
        "shadowsBright": 1.327776,
        "shadowsSpread": 0.135483,
        "highlightsStopsPerUnit": 0.022627,
        "highlightsKnee": 3.506305,
        "highlightsAdapt": 0.872195,
        "highlightsMean": 0.031109,
        "highlightsSpread": 0.190714,
        "white": 1.3021,
        "detailGain": 1.0,
        "meanCentre": -2.38471,
        "spreadCentre": 1.487163,
        "brightCentre": 0.203023,
        "highCentre": -0.288506
      }
    },
    "contrast": {
      "locked": false,
      "form": "two-sided power curve in perceptual space around midpoint with slope a = 2^(contrast*slopePerUnit): below m: m*(p/m)^a, above: 1-(1-m)*((1-p)/(1-m))^a; applied per channel and on luma, mixed by lumaMix",
      "coefficients": {
        "midpoint": 0.4548,
        "slopePerUnit": 0.007384,
        "lumaMix": 0
      }
    },
    "dehaze": {
      "locked": false,
      "form": "the atmospheric model J = (I - A) / t + A, per channel, in linear light (the idea in He, Sun & Tang's dark-channel prior and in darktable's haze removal; no code). A = the airlight, a grey: airlightScale * the photo's anchor high (the 95th percentile of luma, pushed through exposure), or airlight when the anchor has none (synthetic images, flat patches). dark = gaussian blur of min(r, g, b) (radiusFraction of the long edge); haze weight w = min(1, dark / A)^hazePower (hazePower >= 1 keeps a grey ramp monotonic); transmission t = max(minTransmission, 1 - omega * w) with omega = dehaze * omegaPerUnit, capped at 0.95. Below 0 omega is negative: t > 1 and the picture is pulled toward A (haze added). A grey stays grey (A is grey, t is shared by the channels); a pixel at A is a fixed point. Fitted 2026-10-29 on the owner's 43 Death Valley edits that use Dehaze (Tools/parity/fit_edits.py: whole edits, Lightroom's export vs the neutral render; the stage absorbs some of what the other stages get wrong there), held-out mehendi unchanged (2.41 / 7.71). omegaPerUnit sits at its bound. A Dehaze sweep (lr_cc_sweep.py presets --sweep 4) would be the clean development set.",
      "coefficients": {"omegaPerUnit": 0.0095, "airlightScale": 1.30698, "airlight": 1.0, "hazePower": 1.000031, "minTransmission": 0.129031, "radiusFraction": 0.004702}
    },
    "curve": {
      "locked": false,
      "form": "the tone curve, display-referred, per channel in perceptual p = x^(1/gamma): T_c = F_c(M(p)) for p in 0..1, T_c(1) + (p - 1) above. M is the look's all-channels point curve (crv) when set, else the region sliders (tc:dark,mid,light) as the curve through (0,0), (darkAt, darkAt + dark*regionPerUnit), (midAt, midAt + mid*regionPerUnit), (lightAt, lightAt + light*regionPerUnit), (1,1); F_c is the channel's point curve (crvr, crvg, crvb). Every curve is the monotone cubic through its points (Fritsch-Carlson tangents, the page's cSpline; flat beyond its first and last point) after the points' y are made non-decreasing (y_i = max(y_i, y_(i-1))), so no input can make the transfer fall. Rendered as a 256-node lookup per channel, linear between nodes (LookMath.curveTables). Unfitted",
      "coefficients": {
        "regionPerUnit": 0.005,
        "darkAt": 0.25,
        "midAt": 0.5,
        "lightAt": 0.75
      }
    },
    "colour": {
      "locked": false,
      "form": "Oklab chroma: C *= max(0, 1+saturation*saturationPerUnit) * max(0, 1 + vibrance*perUnit*(1-(1-vibranceFloor)*min(1,C/vibranceChromaMax))*(1-skinProtect*skin(h))) ; perUnit = vibrancePerUnit above 0, vibranceDownPerUnit below; skin(h) = exp(-((h-skinHue)/skinWidth)^2), only for vibrance > 0; bw sets C = 0",
      "coefficients": {
        "saturationPerUnit": 0.010109,
        "vibrancePerUnit": 0.007578,
        "vibranceDownPerUnit": 0.011342,
        "vibranceChromaMax": 0.42859,
        "vibranceFloor": 0.22581,
        "skinHue": 31.391,
        "skinWidth": 38.983,
        "skinProtect": 0.83214
      }
    },
    "mixer": {
      "locked": false,
      "form": "the colour mixer, in Oklab (L, C, h): eight bands red, orange, yellow, green, aqua, blue, purple, magenta centred at hueRed .. hueMagenta (degrees, ascending); between two neighbouring centres the upper band's weight is smoothstep of the way across and the lower band's the rest, every other band 0 (the weights sum to 1). With H, S, Lm the look's mixh, mixs, mixl weighted so: h += H*hueDegreesPerUnit; C *= max(0, 1 + S*saturationPerUnit); L *= 1 + Lm*luminancePerUnit*C/(C + luminanceChromaKnee). Every change scales with chroma and a pixel without chroma (C <= 1e-6*L) is returned as it came, so a grey stays the same grey for any values. Centres are the Oklab hues of sRGB's hues 0, 30, 60, 120, 180, 230, 270, 305; unfitted",
      "coefficients": {
        "hueRed": 29,
        "hueOrange": 55,
        "hueYellow": 105,
        "hueGreen": 143,
        "hueAqua": 195,
        "hueBlue": 262,
        "huePurple": 296,
        "hueMagenta": 335,
        "hueDegreesPerUnit": 0.3,
        "saturationPerUnit": 0.01,
        "luminancePerUnit": 0.003,
        "luminanceChromaKnee": 0.05
      }
    },
    "clarity": {
      "locked": false,
      "form": "q = perceptual(luma), base = gaussian blur of q (radiusFraction of the long edge); q += clarity*amountPerUnit*(q-base)*(1-|2q-1|^midtonePower); rgb scaled by the luma ratio",
      "coefficients": {
        "radiusFraction": 0.02,
        "amountPerUnit": 0.01,
        "midtonePower": 2.0
