        "midpointAt0": 0.5,
        "midpointPer100": 0.5,
        "featherAt0": 0.08,
        "featherPer100": 0.6,
        "featherInside": 0.3,
        "rectPower": 8,
        "highlightsPower": 2
      }
    },
    "outputTransform": {
      "locked": false,
      "mapper": "clamp",
      "form": "mapper clamp: clamp to 0..1. mapper sigmoid (LookMath.DisplayMapper; a prototype, measured, not adopted): inset (every primary `inset` of the way to white, turned `rotate` degrees about the grey axis), each channel through a shoulder in log2 around 0.18 (identity up to kneeEV stops above grey; above, L' = kneeEV + H*(1-(1-u)^q) with u = (L-kneeEV)/(maxEV-kneeEV), H = log2(1/0.18)-kneeEV, q = (maxEV-kneeEV)/H: slope 1 at the knee, exactly 1 at maxEV), the middle channel put back between the other two (hueKeep), outset = the inset's inverse, clamp to 0..1. Either way, then: working space to the output space (sRGB preview / export, ProPhoto RGB for parity TIFFs)",
